{"number":13,"title":"Statistics","slug":"statistics","color":"","level":"","estTime":"","description":"Class 9 IMO — Statistics: collecting and presenting grouped and ungrouped data, bar graphs, histograms and frequency polygons, and the mean, median and mode.","topics":[{"title":"Collecting and Presenting Data","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What is Statistics?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Statistics</strong> is the branch of mathematics that deals with the collection, organization, analysis, and interpretation of data. It helps us make sense of information and draw meaningful conclusions.</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What is Data?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Data</strong> is a collection of facts, numbers, or observations. Examples include:</p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>Test scores of students in a class</li><li>Heights of players on a sports team</li><li>Number of cars passing a toll booth each hour</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Types of Data:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Definition</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>**Secondary Data**</td><td>Obtained from published sources</td><td>Data from a government report</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Steps in Data Collection and Presentation:</strong></p><ol class=\"concept-list\"><li><strong>Collect</strong> the data through observation, surveys, or experiments</li><li><strong>Organize</strong> the data in a systematic way</li><li><strong>Present</strong> the data in tables or graphs for easy understanding</li></ol><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Frequency Distribution Table:</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">A <strong>frequency distribution table</strong> shows how often each value (or range of values) occurs in the data.</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Raw Data:</strong> 5, 3, 8, 5, 7, 5, 9, 8, 5, 7, 3, 8, 5, 6, 7</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Frequency Table:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Tally Marks</th><th>Frequency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>5</td><td>IIII</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>I</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>III</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>III</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>I</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>**Total**</td><td></td><td>**15**</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 403\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#eff6ff\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#dbeafe\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Data Collection &amp; Frequency Distribution</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"55\" width=\"580\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Raw Data: Marks of 20 students: 32,45,67,78,56,45,89,67,45,78,90,56,78,45,67,90,56,78,67,89</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Marks</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Tally</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Frequency</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Cumul. Freq</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"610\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#bfdbfe\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"31\" y=\"123\" width=\"578\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#eff6ff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">32</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">I</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9333ea\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1</text><rect x=\"31\" y=\"151\" width=\"578\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">45</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">IIII</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">4</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9333ea\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">5</text><rect x=\"31\" y=\"179\" width=\"578\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#eff6ff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">56</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">III</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">3</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9333ea\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">8</text><rect x=\"31\" y=\"207\" width=\"578\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">67</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">IIII</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">4</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9333ea\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">12</text><rect x=\"31\" y=\"235\" width=\"578\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#eff6ff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">78</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">IIII</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">4</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9333ea\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">16</text><rect x=\"31\" y=\"263\" width=\"578\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">89</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">II</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9333ea\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">18</text><rect x=\"31\" y=\"291\" width=\"578\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#eff6ff\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">90</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">II</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9333ea\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">20</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"338\" width=\"580\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"358\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#92400e\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Class interval groups continuous data (e.g. 30-40, 40-50, ...)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"376\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#78350f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Class width = upper limit − lower limit; Tally marks group in 5s</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Class mark of 20–30?","solution":"(20 + 30) ÷ 2 = 25."},{"number":"2","problem":"Class size of 15.5–20.5?","solution":"20.5 − 15.5 = 5."}],"recap":["Grouped data uses classes and frequencies.","Class mark = (lower + upper) ÷ 2; size = upper − lower."],"quiz":[{"q":"Which of these is the formula for class mark?","options":["(Upper limit − Lower limit)/2","(Upper limit + Lower limit)/2","Upper limit + Lower limit","Upper limit × Lower limit"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Class mark is the exact midpoint of the class interval, calculated as (Upper limit + Lower limit)/2.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"The class mark of the class interval 120 − 150 is:","options":["120","130","135","150"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Class mark = (Lower limit + Upper limit)/2 = (120 + 150)/2 = 270/2 = 135.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"}]},{"title":"Graphs of Data","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What are Graphical Representations?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Graphical representations</strong> are visual ways to display data, making it easier to understand patterns, trends, and comparisons at a glance.</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Types of Graphs:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Graph Type</th><th>Best Used For</th><th>Key Feature</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>**Histogram**</td><td>Showing distribution of continuous data</td><td>Bars touch each other (no gaps)</td></tr><tr><td>**Frequency Polygon**</td><td>Comparing multiple distributions</td><td>Line connecting midpoints</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Bar Graph:</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>Used for <strong>discrete data</strong> (separate categories)</li><li>Bars have equal width with gaps between them</li><li>Height of bar represents frequency</li><li>Can be vertical or horizontal</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Histogram:</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>Used for <strong>continuous data</strong> grouped into class intervals</li><li>Bars touch each other (no gaps)</li><li>Width of bar represents class interval size</li><li>Area of bar represents frequency</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Frequency Polygon:</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>Created by joining the midpoints of histogram bars</li><li>Starts and ends on the x-axis (at frequency 0)</li><li>Useful for comparing two or more data sets on same graph</li></ul><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 460\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#f0fdf4\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#dcfce7\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#16a34a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Measures of Central Tendency</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"55\" width=\"190\" height=\"240\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"95\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">x̄</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Mean</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Sum of all values / Total count</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"172\" width=\"170\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">(32+45+67)/3 = 48</text><rect x=\"225\" y=\"55\" width=\"190\" height=\"240\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fce7f3\" stroke=\"#be185d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"95\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#be185d\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">M</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#be185d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Median</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Middle value when sorted</text><rect x=\"235\" y=\"172\" width=\"170\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#be185d\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">32,45,67 → Median=45</text><rect x=\"430\" y=\"55\" width=\"190\" height=\"240\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"525\" cy=\"95\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#d97706\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"525\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Mo</text><text x=\"525\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#d97706\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Mode</text><text x=\"525\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Most frequently occurring value</text><rect x=\"440\" y=\"172\" width=\"170\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"525\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">32,45,45,67 → Mode=45</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"308\" width=\"600\" height=\"80\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"328\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Median Rules:</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"348\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Odd n: Median = ((n+1)/2)th value</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"368\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Even n: Median = average of (n/2)th and (n/2+1)th values</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"400\" width=\"600\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"418\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">A dataset can have no mode, one mode, or multiple modes (bimodal/multimodal)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"436\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#4b5563\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Empirical relationship: Mode ≈ 3×Median − 2×Mean</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Which graph suits continuous grouped data?","solution":"A histogram (bars are adjacent, no gaps)."},{"number":"2","problem":"A frequency polygon joins which points?","solution":"The midpoints of the tops of the histogram rectangles."}],"recap":["Bar graph: gaps; histogram: adjacent bars, area ∝ frequency.","Frequency polygon joins bar-top midpoints."],"quiz":[{"q":"What is the true class limit for the class interval 10-14 if the next interval starts at 15?","options":["9.5 - 14.5","10 - 15","10.5 - 14.5","9 - 15"],"correct":0,"explanation":"For discontinuous classes, we subtract 0.5 from the lower limit and add 0.5 to the upper limit. So, 9.5 to 14.5.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A tally mark of four vertical lines crossed by a diagonal line represents the number:","options":["4","5","6","10"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A group of five tallies is conventionally drawn as four vertical lines and one diagonal line across them.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"}]},{"title":"Mean, Median and Mode","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What are Measures of Central Tendency?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Measures of central tendency</strong> are single values that describe the \"center\" or \"typical value\" of a data set. The three main measures are mean, median, and mode.</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Mean (Average):</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>Sum of all values divided by the number of values</li><li>Formula: \\(\\bar{x} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of all observations}}{\\text{Number of observations}}\\)</li><li>Most commonly used measure</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Median (Middle Value):</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>The middle value when data is arranged in order</li><li>For odd number of observations: middle value</li><li>For even number of observations: average of two middle values</li><li>Not affected by extreme values (outliers)</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Mode (Most Frequent):</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>The value that occurs most frequently</li><li>A data set can have one mode (unimodal), two modes (bimodal), or no mode</li><li>Useful for categorical data</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Comparison of Measures:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Best Used When</th><th>Affected by Outliers?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Median</td><td>Data has outliers or is skewed</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Mode</td><td>Data is categorical or has repeated values</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 380\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#fdf4ff\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#fae8ff\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#9333ea\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Bar Graph &amp; Histogram</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Bar Graph (Discrete Data)</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"176\" width=\"52\" height=\"104\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Math</text><text x=\"66\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">80</text><rect x=\"112\" y=\"195\" width=\"52\" height=\"84\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#16a34a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"138\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Sci</text><text x=\"138\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#16a34a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">65</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"163\" width=\"52\" height=\"117\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dc2626\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Eng</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">90</text><rect x=\"256\" y=\"215\" width=\"52\" height=\"65\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#d97706\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"282\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Art</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#d97706\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">50</text><line x1=\"25\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"25\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"25\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Score</text><text x=\"480\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9333ea\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Histogram (Continuous Data)</text><rect x=\"335\" y=\"238\" width=\"55\" height=\"42\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#818cf8\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"362\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">30-40</text><rect x=\"390\" y=\"217\" width=\"55\" height=\"63\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#a78bfa\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"417\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">40-50</text><rect x=\"445\" y=\"196\" width=\"55\" height=\"84\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#c084fc\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"472\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">50-60</text><rect x=\"500\" y=\"196\" width=\"55\" height=\"84\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e879f9\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"527\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">60-70</text><rect x=\"555\" y=\"227\" width=\"55\" height=\"52\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f472b6\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"582\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">70-80</text><line x1=\"335\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"610\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"335\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"335\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"308\" width=\"600\" height=\"55\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"328\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#92400e\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Bar Graph: gaps between bars (discrete categories)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"347\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#92400e\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Histogram: NO gaps (continuous data, class intervals)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"364\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#78350f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Area of each bar = Frequency × Class width</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Mean of 4, 6, 8, 10, 12?","solution":"(4+6+8+10+12) ÷ 5 = 40 ÷ 5 = 8."},{"number":"2","problem":"Mode of 2, 3, 3, 5, 3, 7?","solution":"3, since it appears most often."}],"recap":["Mean = sum ÷ count; median = middle value (ordered).","Mode = most frequent; Mode ≈ 3·Median − 2·Mean."],"quiz":[{"q":"A milkman sells milk at ₹50, ₹55, ₹60, and ₹65 per litre in four different localities. If he sells equal quantities in each locality, the mean price is:","options":["₹56","₹57.5","₹58","₹60"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Mean = (50 + 55 + 60 + 65) / 4 = 230 / 4 = ₹57.5.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"A class consists of 15 boys and 10 girls. The average weight of boys is 40 kg and that of girls is 35 kg. The average weight of the whole class is:","options":["37.5 kg","38 kg","38.5 kg","39 kg"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Total weight = (15 × 40) + (10 × 35) = 600 + 350 = 950. Total students = 25. Average = 950/25 = 38 kg.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"hard"}]}],"tests":{"online":{"title":"","minutes":20,"questions":[{"q":"The median of the data 24, 25, 26, x+2, x+3, 30, 31, 34 is 27.5. The value of x is:","options":["25","26","27","28"],"correct":0,"explanation":"n=8. Median = (4th + 5th)/2 = (x+2 + x+3)/2 = (2x+5)/2. So 2x+5 = 55, giving 2x = 50, x = 25.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"The lower class limit of the class 25 - 35 is:","options":["25","30","35","10"],"correct":0,"explanation":"In the interval 25 - 35, the lower class limit is the starting value, which is 25.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Let m be the mid-point and l be the upper limit of a class in a continuous frequency distribution. The lower class limit of the class is:","options":["2m − l","2m + l","m − l","m + 2l"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Mid-point m = (Lower limit + Upper limit)/2. So 2m = Lower + l. Therefore, Lower limit = 2m − l.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"Which of the following is not a measure of central tendency?","options":["Mean","Median","Mode","Range"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Mean, median, and mode measure central tendency. Range measures dispersion.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"The algebraic sum of the deviations of a set of values from their mean is:","options":["0","1","-1","Equal to the mean"],"correct":0,"explanation":"By definition, the sum of deviations of all observations from their mean is always 0. Σ(xᵢ − x̄) = 0.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"In a school, 30 students obtained the following marks: 10 students got 20, 15 got 30, and 5 got 40. The mean score is:","options":["25.5","28.33","30","32.5"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Mean = Σ(fᵢxᵢ) / Σfᵢ = (10×20 + 15×30 + 5×40) / 30 = (200 + 450 + 200) / 30 = 850 / 30 ≈ 28.33.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard","diagram":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 330 205\" width=\"330\" height=\"205\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"geometry figure\"><polygon points=\"63.733333333333334,165 63.733333333333334,85 116.93333333333334,85 116.93333333333334,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"152.40000000000003,165 152.40000000000003,45 205.60000000000002,45 205.60000000000002,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"241.06666666666666,165 241.06666666666666,125 294.26666666666665,125 294.26666666666665,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"165\" x2=\"322\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"90.33333333333334\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text><text x=\"90.33333333333334\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20</text><text x=\"179.00000000000003\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"179.00000000000003\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30</text><text x=\"267.6666666666667\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><text x=\"267.6666666666667\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">40</text></svg>"},{"q":"In a histogram, the area of each rectangle is proportional to:","options":["Class mark","Class size","Class frequency","Cumulative frequency"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The area of a rectangle in a histogram is proportional to the corresponding class frequency.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium","diagram":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 330 205\" width=\"330\" height=\"205\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"geometry figure\"><polygon points=\"46,165 46,105 112.5,105 112.5,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"112.5,165 112.5,45 179,45 179,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"179,165 179,75 245.5,75 245.5,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"245.5,165 245.5,120 312,120 312,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"165\" x2=\"322\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"79.25\" y=\"99\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"79.25\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0–10</text><text x=\"145.75\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><text x=\"145.75\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10–20</text><text x=\"212.25\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"212.25\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20–30</text><text x=\"278.75\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"278.75\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30–40</text></svg>"},{"q":"The mean of the first 5 multiples of 3 is:","options":["6","9","12","15"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The multiples are 3, 6, 9, 12, 15. Sum = 45. Mean = 45/5 = 9.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"In a histogram, the width of the rectangles is proportional to:","options":["Frequencies","Class intervals","Class marks","Cumulative frequencies"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The width of a rectangle in a histogram corresponds to the size of the class interval on the x-axis.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Mean of 20 observations is 15.5. Later it was found that 24 was misread as 42. The corrected mean is:","options":["14.2","14.6","15.0","16.4"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Difference = 24 − 42 = −18. Correct sum = (20 × 15.5) − 18 = 310 − 18 = 292. Correct mean = 292/20 = 14.6.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"If the mean of 6, 4, 7, p, and 10 is 8, then the value of p is:","options":["10","12","13","14"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Mean = (6 + 4 + 7 + p + 10)/5 = 8. So, 27 + p = 40. Therefore, p = 40 − 27 = 13.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A shopkeeper sells 5 shirts of size 38, 12 of size 40, 8 of size 42, and 2 of size 44. The modal shirt size sold is:","options":["38","40","42","44"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Size 40 has the highest frequency (12). Thus, the mode is 40.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy","diagram":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 330 205\" width=\"330\" height=\"205\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"geometry figure\"><polygon points=\"59.3,165 59.3,115 99.19999999999999,115 99.19999999999999,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"125.8,165 125.8,45 165.7,45 165.7,165\" fill=\"rgba(240,130,30,0.45)\" stroke=\"#f0821e\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"192.3,165 192.3,85 232.20000000000002,85 232.20000000000002,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"258.8,165 258.8,145 298.7,145 298.7,165\" fill=\"rgba(31,58,95,0.18)\" stroke=\"#1f3a5f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"165\" x2=\"322\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"79.25\" y=\"109\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><text x=\"79.25\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">38</text><text x=\"145.75\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"145.75\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">40</text><text x=\"212.25\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><text x=\"212.25\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">42</text><text x=\"278.75\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"278.75\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#333\" text-anchor=\"middle\">44</text></svg>"},{"q":"In a cricket match, Virat scored 45, 60, 30, 85, and 80 runs in 5 innings. What is the median of his scores?","options":["60","45","80","85"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Arranged in order: 30, 45, 60, 80, 85. The middle value (3rd term) is 60.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"A taxi driver in Delhi earns ₹500, ₹450, ₹600, ₹400, and ₹550 in 5 days. What is the median earning?","options":["₹450","₹500","₹550","₹600"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Arranging in ascending order: 400, 450, 500, 550, 600. The median (middle value) is ₹500.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"The weights of 5 students in kg are 42, 45, 48, 51, 54. The range of their weights is:","options":["10","11","12","15"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Range = Maximum value − Minimum value = 54 − 42 = 12.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"}]}}}